---
/**
 * foodcraft / FaqBO — "Sipsip Tea Bar" (BO), the FAQ band
 * (design element data-component="FAQ").
 *
 * ROLE: the page's one plain-answer band. A CENTRED head — a lilac pill eyebrow
 * over one Baloo 2 headline — sits above a TWO-COLUMN masonry-free grid of
 * white rounded cards, each holding a question and its answer, every answer
 * drawn OPEN. There is no accordion: the design draws all six cards expanded,
 * and on a drinks-counter page the answers ARE the practicalities. Someone
 * standing on the pavement deciding whether to walk in should not have to click
 * to find out. Nothing here is ruled and nothing here is sharp — the card's own
 * radius is the only edge in the band.
 *
 * THE DESIGN IS THE SPECIFICATION. Every value below is lifted verbatim from
 * "Sipsip Tea Bar Landing.dc.html":
 *   section    id="faq" (kept verbatim) · padding 76px 28px 0
 *   head       text-align center · margin-bottom 30px
 *   eyebrow    inline-block PILL · 11px / 700 / .14em / uppercase ·
 *              colour #5C3580 on an #EEE2F5 ground · padding 8px 16px ·
 *              radius 100px                            → the wrapper's .kick
 *   headline   Baloo 2 700 · clamp(30px,4vw,52px) / 1.08 · margin .24em 0 0 ·
 *              #241A22                                 → the wrapper's .h2
 *   grid       repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)) · gap 14px
 *   card       #FFFFFF ground · radius 22px · padding 24px 26px
 *   question   Baloo 2 600 · 20px · margin 0 0 8px · #241A22
 *   answer     14.5px / 1.78 · #5D5158 · margin 0
 *
 * ONE TYPOGRAPHIC VALUE HERE IS NOT THE DESIGN'S, and it is stated rather than
 * left to be discovered: the design writes NO letter-spacing on ANY heading —
 * not on this h2, not on this h3, not on the hero h1 — while PageBO pins
 * :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) AND :where(.h2) to -.01em for the whole template. That
 * tracking is deliberately NOT overridden here. It is the wrapper's shared
 * display treatment, worn by every heading on the page, and unpicking it in one
 * band would leave this headline tracking differently from the ones above and
 * below it to buy back -.52px at the 52px cap and -.2px on the 20px question.
 * The divergence is the WRAPPER's to reverse across all fifteen sections at
 * once, not this band's to fork; it is recorded here so a reader diffing this
 * file against the design finds it already answered.
 *
 * R1 · NO LITERAL HEX. Every hex the design writes here is used through the
 * PageBO token holding the SAME value:
 *   #EEE2F5 --lilac · #5C3580 --accent-deep · #241A22 --ink · #FFFFFF --card
 *   #5D5158 --ink-soft · #7B4FA8 --accent (owner links only) · 100px --r-pill
 * ONE VALUE HAS NO TOKEN and is reported rather than invented: the card's 22px
 * corner. --r-md is 18px and --r-lg is 26px, so no token holds 22, and this is a
 * LENGTH, not a colour — R1 governs colour. Rounding to either neighbour would
 * be a different drawing on the only shape this band is made of, so the design's
 * number stands, exactly as TrustBO keeps the same 22px on the design's other
 * small white card and CredentialsBO keeps its 32px plate and 20px cell.
 *
 * THE THREE HUES. This band touches the LILAC only, and only as the eyebrow
 * pill's ground with the design's own deep purple on it. It renders no --pink
 * and no --sage at all, so the pairing this palette cannot survive — --accent on
 * --pink, 3.93:1 — cannot arise here. It also declares no band class: the design
 * leaves the FAQ on the page's blush ground and floats white cards on it, so
 * there is no ground/text pair for this section to opt into. The white-on-blush
 * card is a QUIET step (--card #FFFFFF against --paper #FFF7F2) and that is the
 * design's intent — the cards are separated by their corners, not by contrast.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS — all four DECLARED in components/editor/genericContentSchema.ts
 * under section id 'faq'. A data-field on any other path is a dead hook that no
 * sidebar input owns, so nothing outside this list is bound:
 *   faq.tag             — the eyebrow pill
 *   faq.headline        — the h2. Rendered with set:html so an owner can put
 *                         this template's PURPLE COLOUR EMPHASIS anywhere inside
 *                         their own sentence. That <em> rule is global in PageBO
 *                         on purpose: scoped styles cannot reach markup made by
 *                         set:html (R3), so an emphasis rule written here would
 *                         never apply. Note the emphasis is a COLOUR CHANGE and
 *                         not an italic — Baloo 2 ships no italic, and asking
 *                         for one synthesises an oblique that fights its rounded
 *                         terminals.
 *   faq.items.${i}.q    — the question
 *   faq.items.${i}.a    — the answer, also set:html so an owner can emphasise,
 *                         bold or link inside their own sentence
 *
 * SHAPE TOLERANCE, read but never hooked: the schema declares faq.items with
 * fallbackPaths ['faq'], so the stored value is legitimately EITHER
 * {tag, headline, items:[…]} or a bare ARRAY; and legacy submissions spell the
 * pair {question, answer} where the schema and every current writer spell
 * {q, a}. Both shapes are read, but the data-field hook ALWAYS spells
 * faq.items.${i}.q / .a — that is the path the sidebar input owns, so the first
 * edit heals a legacy row onto the schema key instead of writing a third shape.
 *
 * DERIVED (computed here, never authored here): only `rows` — the surviving
 * question/answer pairs, each still carrying its ORIGINAL array index (R6) — and
 * the two .reveal wrappers with their single data-delay step. Nothing in this
 * band is numbered, badged or railed, so R6's decorative-DISPLAY-index half has
 * nothing here to apply to; its original-index half does, and is honoured.
 *
 * R2 · NOT ONE WORD IS SUPPLIED BY THIS FILE, and on an FAQ that rule bites
 * harder than anywhere else on the page: an answer is a PROMISE about a business
 * this template has never visited. So there is no opening or closing time, no
 * "last order thirty minutes before close", no sugar-level or ice-level scale,
 * no dairy-free / lactose claim, no allergen statement, no wifi, no power
 * outlet, no seating or laptop policy, no delivery radius, no minimum order, no
 * card-versus-cash line, no "we reply within…", and no example question. The
 * design's own demo strings ("Good to know", "Asked a lot" and its six sample
 * rows) are the DESIGNER filling in their own template. Every guard sits OUTSIDE
 * its tag, so an empty value removes the ELEMENT and not merely its text: no
 * empty eyebrow pill, no headline over nothing, no empty <h3> holding open 8px
 * of margin above a blank line box, and — because the card IS its own white
 * plate — no plate drawn around a row that is not there.
 * NO STAR ROW EXISTS HERE, and that is a rule rather than an omission. The
 * schema exposes no numeric rating anywhere on faq.*, so there is no field this
 * band could clamp to 1–5 and draw; five stars over someone who gave no rating
 * is a fabricated claim. That treatment belongs to TESTIMONIALS, where it is
 * drawn only from a numeric rating, clamped, aria-hidden, with the number itself
 * in the accessible label — and where a review with no rating gets a plain rule
 * instead. An FAQ row has nothing to stand in for, so it gets no rule either.
 *
 * SECTION GATE (R5) — IT COUNTS THE CARDS, never the tag and never the headline.
 * lib/derive-content-defaults.ts hard-codes faq.tag to 'Good to know' and
 * faq.headline to 'Questions, answered' on EVERY site, while emitting items only
 * when the submission actually answered something. A gate on tag || headline
 * would therefore ship a centred 52px headline standing over an empty grid on
 * any shop whose owner typed no questions. With no filled row the whole
 * <section> is omitted — no eyebrow, no headline, no grid, no card and no
 * padding.
 *
 * ROW GUARDS: a card is kept when EITHER field has content, and the two tags are
 * guarded independently. Silently vanishing an answer an owner typed is a worse
 * failure than printing a lone paragraph inside a card. Fields are TRIMMED
 * before they are tested, because a value holding only a space is truthy and
 * would print exactly that empty element.
 *
 * DELIBERATELY NOT RENDERED, so none of it reads as an oversight:
 *   · NO onPage() ANCHOR HELPER AND NO PAGE_ANCHORS SET (R7). The helper exists
 *     to rewrite an owner's href onto the ids this page really has — for BO that
 *     set is `menu about gallery visit faq main`, with location/contact → visit,
 *     services/rooms → menu, host/why → about, work → gallery, book → main, and
 *     tel: / mailto: / http passing through untouched. This band emits NO href
 *     of any kind: no button, no link, no data-href-field, because the design
 *     gives the FAQ no action at all. A remap helper with no call site is dead
 *     code a later reader would have to prove unused, which is what a reviewer
 *     flags instead — so it is not carried, exactly as AreaBO, TrustBO, AboutBO
 *     and FaqBM each record for the same reason. The one anchor this file owns
 *     is its own id="faq", already in that set and already what HeaderBO's nav
 *     links to.
 *   · no <details>/<summary> accordion, per the design (see ROLE).
 *   · no button and no CTA. The order action lives in the header, the hero, the
 *     CTA band and the footer, exactly where the design places it.
 *   · no card border and no hairline. The design gives the card a ground and a
 *     corner and nothing else; a 1px --line edge would read as a second, weaker
 *     rectangle inside the corner it is meant to trace.
 *   · no .plate, no role="img" and no aria-hidden anywhere (R9). This band
 *     renders no image, no upload and no decorative glyph, so there is no
 *     element to give an accessible name and none to hide from the tree. No
 *     accessibility attribute in this file is conditional, so there is no way
 *     for a literal one to be duplicated beside a conditional one.
 *   · no data-block marker: editorBridge only needs one where two content
 *     prefixes share a <section>. This band is faq.* alone, so the Blocks toggle
 *     resolves to it by hook weight already.
 *
 * SECTION PADDING IS THE WRAPPER'S, not this file's, and that is a decision. The
 * design writes `padding:76px 28px 0`: the 1200/28px half is the shared .wrap,
 * and PageBO's `section { padding: clamp(48px,6.4vw,80px) 0 }` renders 76.8px at
 * a 1200px viewport and meets the design's 76px exactly at 1187.5px — i.e. this
 * design's own 76px IS the wrapper's shared step at the width the design was
 * drawn to. The design's bottom-0 is a WHOLE-PAGE rhythm decision (every unbanded
 * section in that document pads top only) which belongs in the wrapper, so no
 * local override is written. CredentialsBO and AboutBO flagged the identical
 * mismatch and left it to the wrapper; so does this file.
 *
 * R3 — one scoped <style>, no is:global. Both the headline and the answers
 * arrive through set:html, so scoped rules cannot reach inside them: the
 * headline's purple <em> is PageBO's global :where(.h2 em), and an <em>,
 * <strong> or <a> inside an answer is reached from here via :global().
 *
 * VERIFIED CONTRAST — COMPUTED (sRGB relative luminance, WCAG 2.x) from the
 * hexes PageBO declares, not estimated. Nothing in this band is below AA:
 *   eyebrow  --accent-deep on --lilac ....... 7.40
 *   headline --ink on --paper .............. 15.92
 *   question --ink on --card ............... 16.86
 *   answer   --ink-soft on --card ........... 7.54
 *   an owner's link --accent on --card ...... 5.96
 * --muted is not used in this band at all. Neither is --accent on --pink, the
 * one pairing this palette fails at 3.93 — see THE THREE HUES above.
 */
// `layout` is accepted because PageBO passes it to every section uniformly.
// This band reads nothing outside content.*, so it is never destructured.
interface Props { content: any; layout?: any; }
const { content } = Astro.props;

// The schema declares 'faq.items' with fallbackPaths ['faq'], so the stored
// value is legitimately EITHER {tag, headline, items:[…]} or a bare array.
// Both shapes are read; only an OBJECT can carry a tag or a headline.
const faqRaw = content.faq;
const faq = faqRaw && !Array.isArray(faqRaw) ? faqRaw : {};
const tag = (faq.tag || '').trim();
const headline = (faq.headline || '').trim();

// Legacy submissions spell the pair {question, answer}; the schema (and every
// current writer) spells {q, a}. Read both — but the data-field hook below
// always spells q / a, which is the path the sidebar input owns.
type Item = { q?: string; a?: string; question?: string; answer?: string };
const items: Item[] = Array.isArray(faq.items)
  ? faq.items
  : Array.isArray(faqRaw)
    ? (faqRaw as Item[])
    : [];

// Optional chaining, not a bare read: a stored list can carry a null slot (a row
// deleted by an older editor left a hole), and reading `.q` off it would throw
// at BUILD time and take the whole site down, not just this band.
const qOf = (it: Item): string => it?.q ?? it?.question ?? '';
const aOf = (it: Item): string => it?.a ?? it?.answer ?? '';

// R6 — carry the ORIGINAL index past the blank filter, so removing question 2
// cannot misdirect an edit of question 3 into question 2.
const rows = items
  .map((it, i: number) => ({ i, q: qOf(it).trim(), a: aOf(it).trim() }))
  .filter((r) => Boolean(r.q || r.a));

// With neither eyebrow nor headline the head block would spend 30px of margin on
// nothing, so it is omitted whole rather than rendered empty.
const hasHead = Boolean(tag || headline);
---
{rows.length > 0 && (
  <section class="sip-faq" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      {hasHead && (
        <div class="sip-faq-head reveal">
          {tag && <span class="kick sip-faq-kick" data-field="faq.tag">{tag}</span>}
          {headline && <h2 class="h2 sip-faq-h" data-field="faq.headline" set:html={headline}></h2>}
        </div>
      )}
      <div class="sip-faq-grid reveal" data-delay="1">
        {rows.map((row) => (
          <div class="sip-faq-card">
            {row.q && <h3 class="sip-faq-q" data-field={`faq.items.${row.i}.q`}>{row.q}</h3>}
            {row.a && <p class="sip-faq-a" data-field={`faq.items.${row.i}.a`} set:html={row.a}></p>}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

<style>
  /* The band keeps PageBO's shared section padding and the page's blush ground:
     the design declares no background here, and the white cards ARE the
     figure/ground step (see the frontmatter note on SECTION PADDING).
     min-width:0 so a long unbroken word inside a card can never widen the grid
     and push the page sideways (R8). */
  .sip-faq { min-width: 0; }

  /* Design: text-align center, margin-bottom 30px. That is the whole head rule —
     the pill and the headline bring their own type. */
  .sip-faq-head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* THE EYEBROW. The wrapper's .kick already carries this design's type — 11px,
     700, uppercase, inline-block, line-height 1.1 — and owns the whole size
     curve (it steps to 10.5px at 520), so no font-size is written here. What
     .kick does NOT know is that in THIS band the eyebrow is a PILL on the blush:
     the lilac ground, the deep-purple label, 8px/16px of padding and the 100px
     corner. Those four and the design's .14em tracking (the wrapper's base is
     .18em; its own 520 step lands on the same .14em, so nothing moves there) are
     all that is restated. The label is --accent-deep and not --accent because
     that is what the design writes, and it is the darker of the two, which this
     pale lilac pill wants: 7.40 against 4.77 for --accent on this SAME
     lilac ground. Both are computed here rather than carried over — the
     wrapper's 5.63 is --accent on --paper, which is a different ground and
     not the comparison this pill makes.
     .kick is an inline-block, so max-width:100% is what bounds one long
     owner-typed word at 360px (R8). Qualified by the head so it out-specifies
     the wrapper's :where() primitive whatever order the sheets land in. */
  .sip-faq-head .sip-faq-kick {
    letter-spacing: .14em;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    background-color: var(--lilac);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* Design: Baloo 2 700 · clamp(30px,4vw,52px) / 1.08 · margin .24em 0 0. Face,
     weight and colour are already the shared .h2's; only the size, the leading
     and the margins are this band's. The margin runs ABOVE the headline and not
     below it, because the 30px gap to the grid is the head block's own
     margin-bottom, not the headline's.

     max-width:none — the design's FAQ h2 carries NO measure cap and is CENTRED.
     Leaving the wrapper's 22ch in place would be visibly wrong here rather than
     merely tighter: a 22ch block box sits at the START of its line box, so the
     text would centre inside a box that is itself parked on the left. Releasing
     it cannot push the page sideways because this rule carries
     overflow-wrap:anywhere (R8).

     THE CLAMP LADDER, traced ACROSS BREAKPOINTS because two audits in this
     family found type that GREW as the viewport narrowed:
       1300px+ .. 52px (cap)  ·  1200px .. 48px  ·  900px .. 36px
       760px .. 30.4px  ·  750px and below .. 30px (floor), flat from there
     No media query in this file restates this size, so that ramp is the whole of
     it: it only ever DECREASES as the viewport narrows and never goes under the
     design's own floor. The wrapper's 760 `:where(.h2)` STEP DOWN to
     clamp(26px,7vw,29px) is (0,1,1) and loses to this (0,4,0) rule, which is the
     intent — that rule's own max-width:none and overflow-wrap:anywhere are
     restated here, so nothing is lost by winning. */
  .sip-faq-head .sip-faq-h {
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 52px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: .24em 0 0;
    max-width: none;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* Design: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)) · gap 14px. minmax(0,…) on BOTH tracks is
     what lets a card shrink instead of overflowing — an `auto` minimum would let
     one long word set the column width. */
  .sip-faq-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* Design: #FFFFFF ground · radius 22px · padding 24px 26px. No token holds
     22px — --r-md is 18px and --r-lg is 26px — and this is a length, not a
     colour, so the design's number stands (see R1 in the block above). No
     border: the design gives this card a ground and a corner and nothing else.
     NO alignment property is written: a grid item stretches to its row by
     default, so two cards side by side already share a height — which is the
     design's own drawing — and a block container already starts its content at
     the top, so an `align-content` here would be a declaration that changes
     nothing. */
  .sip-faq-card {
    background-color: var(--card);
    border-radius: 22px;
    padding: 24px 26px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* Design: Baloo 2 600 · 20px · margin 0 0 8px · #241A22. PageBO sets
     :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) to Baloo 2 700 --ink at line-height 1.12 with -.01em
     tracking. The face and colour are the design's already; the WEIGHT is not —
     the design steps this h3 down to 600, which is the difference between a
     question and a section head — so 600 is stated.
     line-height is stated as `normal` because that is literally what the design
     renders: its h3 carries no line-height and its stylesheet sets none. Picking
     a number would be a divergence, and inheriting the wrapper's 1.12 would be a
     VISIBLE one the moment an owner's question runs longer than the designer's
     and wraps — at 1.12 Baloo 2's generous descenders crowd the caps of the next
     line.
     QUALIFIED BY THE CARD, which records the rule this one beats rather than
     being what makes it win. This project builds on Astro 5 with the default
     scopedStyleStrategy 'attribute', so the scope compiles to
     `[data-astro-cid-…]` on EVERY compound — worth (0,1,0) each, not the
     nothing a `:where()` scope would contribute. A bare `.sip-faq-q` therefore
     weighs (0,2,0) and already beats PageBO's `html[data-page="BO"]
     :where(h1,h2,h3,h4)` at (0,1,1); the two-class form written here is (0,4,0)
     and wins by more. Either way the question renders at the design's
     600/normal rather than the wrapper's 700/1.12 — but the qualification is
     what keeps that true if the strategy is ever moved to 'where', where a bare
     class would drop to (0,1,0) and silently lose. */
  .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-q {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: normal;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* Design: 14.5px / 1.78 · #5D5158 · margin 0. Deliberately NOT the wrapper's
     .body primitive: .body clamps 14.5px UP to 15.5px and sets 1.72 leading,
     and this design pins the run flat at 14.5/1.78. Qualified by the card so it
     clears PageBO's `:where(p){margin:0 0 1em}` at (0,1,1) — an unqualified
     class would win too, but the card-scoped form documents which rule it is
     beating. */
  .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-a {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.78;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* The answer arrives through set:html, so scoped rules cannot reach inside it
     (R3). An owner's emphasis keeps the answer's own colour: the purple on a
     14.5px run inside a paragraph reads as a link that does not work — this
     template's purple emphasis is the HEADLINE's signature and stays there. */
  .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-a :global(em),
  .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-a :global(i) { font-style: italic; color: inherit; }
  .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-a :global(strong),
  .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-a :global(b) { font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  /* An owner who pastes a link into an answer gets the purple, underlined on
     hover only — the same restraint as the wrapper's .linkc and the same reason:
     a colour that does not move mid-interaction cannot fail a contrast check
     halfway through one. --accent on --card is 5.96, above AA. */
  .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-a :global(a) {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-a :global(a:hover) {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* 900 — this band's OWN grid, which is the part R8 leaves to this file. Two
     cards of 24/26px padding inside a 92vw wrap run out of measure before the
     type does, so the tracks fold to one and the cards stack. The 14px gutter is
     kept: it is already the design's tightest gap and a stacked column wants the
     same breath a row does. NO font-size is touched here — the headline's base
     clamp is already handing over 36px at this width, and any cap written below
     that number would make it JUMP as the viewport crossed 900px. */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .sip-faq-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }

  /* 520 — nothing may push the page sideways. Every track is already
     minmax(0,…) and every string in here breaks anywhere, so what is left is
     spacing and one type step, and every one of them is strictly SMALLER than
     the value above it, so the ladder stays monotonic:
       head margin 30 → 24 · card padding 24/26 → 22/20 · question 20 → 19
     The ANSWER is not re-sized: 14.5px is already this design's floor for body
     copy and the wrapper's .body clamp bottoms out at the same number, so a
     smaller step here would be this file inventing a size the design never
     writes.
     THE HEADLINE IS NOT RE-CLAMPED HERE either. Its own clamp reaches the
     design's 30px FLOOR at 750px and holds flat from there down — that floor is
     the design's own answer for a narrow viewport, and restating a clamp inside
     a max-width query is the exact construct that shipped a headline which GREW
     as the viewport narrowed on an earlier template in this family. The measure
     is handled too: this file already sets max-width:none, so the wrapper's 760
     `max-width:none` has nothing left to add, and overflow-wrap:anywhere covers
     an owner headline longer than the designer's at any width. */
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .sip-faq-head { margin-bottom: 24px; }
    .sip-faq-card { padding: 22px 20px; }
    .sip-faq-card .sip-faq-q { font-size: 19px; }
  }
</style>
